{
  "name": "l0_should_toggle",
  "about": "`CBaseEntity::ShouldToggle` 0x100a98f0 (`int ShouldToggle(int useType, int state)`, `RET 8`; not a vtable slot, reached through the thunk 0x100076a3 by `CLight::Use` 0x10130580, `CSprite::Use` 0x1042f030 and `FUN_10159700`; `walks/L0-r020.md`). After the scope-trace push the arms run in this order: `useType == 3` (TOGGLE) -> 1 (`100a995b`); `useType == 2` (SET) -> 1 (`100a9960`); `state != 0` (`TEST ECX,ECX`, any bit): `useType == 1` (ON) -> 0, else 1 (`100a9969`-`100a9970`); `state == 0`: `useType != 0` -> 1, `useType == 0` (OFF) -> 0 (`100a9984`-`100a9986`). Accept is `MOV EAX,1; RET 8`, reject `XOR EAX,EAX; RET 8`; nothing is written. The whole table over useType in {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, -1} and state in {0, 1, 2, -1} is probed on a `logic_relay` created at runtime (the predicate reads `this` for the trace label only); states 2 and -1 act as on. The in-play door is `CSprite::Use` on an `env_sprite` born on (`spawnflags 1`): `state = (m_fEffects != 0x40)`, so ON on the lit sprite is refused (`result=0`, `arm=refused`), OFF turns it off, OFF again is refused, TOGGLE turns it on. Reported as `fail`, a cell of the table or a sprite arm differs from retail's.",
  "stage": "arena",
  "seed": 1,
  "duration": 1.6,
